Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:17:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Seats made in parallel no longer collide on the first free
 number

POST /admin/test-accounts took the first free fictional number without a lock,
so parallel calls all picked the same one, clashed on the unique phone key,
and past three retries answered 500 (the tester's 60292). An auto-picked seat
now takes a transaction-scoped advisory lock, picks its number and writes it
inside one transaction, so the next caller picks after it. A number the caller
chose is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
